@@ -186,6 +186,31 @@ information about the syntax of the templating language. The Jinja syntax is
 powerful, and we recommend you take some time to read their documentation if you
 are building complex prompts.
 
+### Custom filters
+
+Custom Jinja filters can be attached to a prompt without changing filters used
+by other prompts. Pass a mapping from template names to callables to the
+decorator, `Prompt.from_str`, or `Prompt.from_file`:
+
+```python
+import outlines
+
+def surround(value, left, right):
+    return f"{left}{value}{right}"
+
+@outlines.prompt(filters={"surround": surround})
+def tagged_prompt(text):
+    """{{ text | surround("<", ">") }}"""
+
+tagged_prompt("example")  # '<example>'
+```
+
+A custom filter overrides a Jinja or Outlines filter with the same name for
+that prompt only. Use `prompt.with_filters({...})` to derive another prompt
+with additional or replacement filters. The original prompt is unchanged, and
+derivation may be chained. Passing `None` or an empty mapping keeps the current
+filters. File prompts retain relative includes and template inheritance.
+
 
 ## Tools
 
